{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-9-21","kind":"proposition","title":"偶数之和仍为偶数","englishTitle":"If as many even numbers as we please be added together, the whole is even.","book":9,"number":21,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.21","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:9.prop.21/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":21,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-9-21@raw-0759dfcfa20eb019","contentId":"euclid-9-21","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0759dfcfa20eb01925c24f55c0f09274d1917742c5f703c42327fed8330d19ca","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-9-21.statement","euclid-9-21.construction.1","euclid-9-21.proof.1","euclid-9-21.conclusion","euclid-9-21.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-9-21.statement","contentId":"euclid-9-21","revisionId":"euclid-9-21@raw-0759dfcfa20eb019","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"73f783629b3c14db10674806fdba75a146b0938ec7ff0770df98a39f7cd52ec6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If as many even numbers as we please be added together, the whole is even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果能把我们想要的 数字加在一起 整个数字是公平的"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-21.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-9-21","revisionId":"euclid-9-21@raw-0759dfcfa20eb019","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0e774769c8863b946e917427581c0204b9f98a561a51472ee504c48f84b55dab","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let as many even numbers as we please, AB, BC, CD, DE, be added together; I say that the whole AE is even."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让我们想多就多,就加AB,BC,CD,DE;我说,整个AE是均衡的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-21.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-9-21","revisionId":"euclid-9-21@raw-0759dfcfa20eb019","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9b9e107f78e65e1cd1940a80acff9c4a65148ce34118ff300aa8aa402d54c517","citations":["euclid-7-def-6"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, since each of the numbers AB, BC, CD, DE is even, it has a half part; [[VII. Def. 6](/principles/euclid-7-def-6)] so that the whole AE also has a half part."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为AB中每一个都平了,BC,CD,DE,因此,整个AE也各占一半。 [[VII. Def. 6](/principles/euclid-7-def-6)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-21.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-9-21","revisionId":"euclid-9-21@raw-0759dfcfa20eb019","order":3,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"882e7fdefd3fe3aafd09dc024e23c57f8276264380b160200327d2ff2e59b627","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But an even number is that which is divisible into two equal parts; [id.] therefore AE is even. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但一个偶数是可分为两个相等部分的数,因此,AE是Q,E,D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-9-21.source","contentId":"euclid-9-21","revisionId":"euclid-9-21@raw-0759dfcfa20eb019","order":4,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c77ecc4404cd58dbcb26594700ecf98c9afd793fcb97d7c96b4d27c828fa44f9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"pr